## CONTINUE HANDLER vs EXIT HANDLER

```sql
-- CONTINUE: ejecuta handler y continúa
DECLARE CONTINUE HANDLER FOR 1062
  SELECT 'Error: duplicado' AS error;

-- EXIT: ejecuta handler y abandona el bloque BEGIN...END
DECLARE EXIT HANDLER FOR SQLEXCEPTION
BEGIN
  ROLLBACK;
  SELECT 'Error: transacción revertida' AS error;
END;
```

> **Regla**: CONTINUE para errores recuperables, EXIT para errores fatales.

## Handler + transacciones: ROLLBACK en error

```sql
DELIMITER //

CREATE PROCEDURE sp_transferir_nota(
  IN p_origen INT, IN p_destino INT, IN p_cantidad DECIMAL(4,2)
)
BEGIN
  DECLARE EXIT HANDLER FOR SQLEXCEPTION
  BEGIN
    ROLLBACK;
    SELECT 'Error: transferencia revertida' AS resultado;
  END;

  START TRANSACTION;
  UPDATE notas SET nota = nota - p_cantidad WHERE id = p_origen;
  UPDATE notas SET nota = nota + p_cantidad WHERE id = p_destino;
  COMMIT;
  SELECT 'Transferencia completada' AS resultado;
END //

DELIMITER ;
```

